Your notes are strong and clear. They are not a polish pass.

They are a complete homepage revision — architecture, visual system, navigation, and several new section treatments. Specifically:

1. Dark-first visual system (charcoal/black + cream type) instead of the current light Culture Club canvas as the primary homepage environment
2. Left navigation drawer (~28% width, ALD-style) replacing the full-screen overlay
3. Horizontal opening carousel (01 → 02 → 03 → 04) replacing the vertical chapter stack — then vertical scroll only after that
4. Four Pillars as one full-screen frame with four equal vertical divisions (all visible at once)
5. New vertical homepage flow after the carousel: What We Offer → The Space → Membership → Start Here → Footer
6. New / redesigned treatments: What We Offer gateway, passport/credential Membership section, simplified dark footer, updated CTA language, larger type scale, header format updates, and mixed cinematic media for the opening

That’s a rebuild of the homepage experience on top of the foundation — not spacing, typos, or small mechanism fixes.

